{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/93906-one-more-trick-a-hunter-fiction","id":93906,"title":"One More Trick - a hunter fiction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-18T16:31:35-07:00","id":93906,"title":"One More Trick - a hunter fiction","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Maria Carcione was scared, really scared. She wanted to believe this was just another hunt, but she would never go on a normal hunt with somebody she didn\u2019t trust. That was before she saw the gnawed bones, centuries of missing kids, before she heard about what he was up against. That is why her men were sharing a firing position with a cell she\u2019d never even heard of, some yuppie-guilt chicks from Bryn Mawr. At least they held those weapons like they knew how to use them. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">It was Doug who first set eyes upon The Hag, as soon as he even thought about aiming a shot she knew. In a second the old woman had transformed into a murder of crows. Doug laid into them with a burst of automatic gunfire, the two cells quickly followed suit, as did hunters hidden in other buildings. Under attack from all sides the crows began to drop like wheat before the harvest. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">One of the yuppies pulled out an old leather bound tome and began chanting something in Welsh. \u201cI knew it\u201d, thought Maria. She was working with a witch, but to her own surprise she didn\u2019t care. Not when she remembered the fear in the Irish priest\u2019s voice as she blessed them before the battle, or the look on those creepy Germans\u2019 faces when they voted to unlock a chest full of amulets. If the people Maria thought had a clue were resorting desperate measures, so could she. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">One second Cynthia was half way though her spell, the next she was looking in surprise at The Hag with her throat slit. The ancient faerie took hold of Cynthia\u2019s blood and pulled, in an instant eight pints flowed through a small wound in defiance of geometry. \u201cA virgin, at mothering age?\u201d The Hag gave a hideous laugh that combined the worst of a teenager\u2019s mocking giggle with a witch\u2019s cackle. \u201cWhat nonsense are they pouring into your head where The Art should go?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Maria tried to shoot her, but the moment The Hag appeared both cells discovered that their guns had transformed into serpents which were rather intent on killing them. The Hag departed to a background of guns firing at illusionary ravens and hunters fighting their own weapons. She took with her Cynthia\u2019s blood, and Cynthia\u2019s magic. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Johnny McDermot gripped his rifle in anticipation, today was his big chance to prove himself. He had mixed feelings about the duty he and his team had been given: guarding one of the four stones that prevented The Hag from escaping. It was important work and this secret was the hounds contribution to the alliance, but if all went according to plan he wouldn\u2019t see any action. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Then he heard gunfire, sustained gunfire, things had not gone according to plan. Without a word the warriors tensed, ready for battle. The thought of facing an unseele cailleach was making battle hardened men sweat. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Enormous manikins formed of mud, vine and asphalt charged. The hag followed behind yelling threats and encouragement, but it was all for naught. The hunters had placed their defences well, they had clear firing lines and iron bullets. It was only when Johnny heard a human scream that he realised this attack was something other than an act of desperation. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The cailleach shouldn\u2019t have been able to travel beyond the warding stone, and the same ban bound all her creatures but somehow a band of goblins had attacked the hunters from the rear. With a chorus of battle cries the humans dropped their guns and raised iron in defence. Both parties fought with superhuman skill, but cold iron swords parted crabshell armour as though it were air while the hunter\u2019s own armour held true. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Brother Larry tried to radio a warning to the other cells and was struck in the thigh for his troubles. Johnny stood over the fallen priest striking at anyone who came near while Larry took shots with his pistol. Robert was surrounded and went down fighting. Patrick wielded his spear one handed, keeping his opponents beyond arms reach then picking them off with his gun. The hunters fought their way to a painful bloody victory, killing, capturing and driving off their attackers. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Reverend Benjamin heard the Irishman\u2019s warning over his radio. He heard the gunfire soften as hunters began to fortify their positions against a direction thought safe. His congregation did not, if they were true to their duty The Lord would keep them safe from Satan\u2019s pet whore. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">From their hiding place the cell saw their prey bustle past, flanked by two of her hulking manikins. With a shout of \u201cPraise Jesus!\u201d they lept into action. Carter and Jesse hung taking shot after shot but the mankins closed ranks to shield their creator with their lives. Benjamin charged with a pistol in one hand and a chain of white lilies in the other, he shouldered the dying manakins aside and threw his chain around The Hags neck while unloading his pistol into her chest. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI\u2019ve taken your magic, surrender whore!\u201d as quick as a snake The Hags bony fingers closed around Benjamin\u2019s neck \u201cOnly </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">my</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> magic poppet\u201d. With a quiet snap another candle was snuffed out. Carter and Jesse tried to finish the hunt, but the Hag used Benjamin\u2019s body, and his body armour, to shield herself as she retreated into the sewers. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Though she was wounded by iron, the cailleach was far from death. She hobbled down the sewer to put as much distance between herself and pursuit. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pursuit was not long in coming. Five hunters lead by Carter and Jessie descended into the sewers. The hag was waiting, she reached into her rags and brought out an moleskin pouch. With a flick of the wrist she opened it, unleashing the wind within. The hunters were thrown down the sewer, landing in a heap of broken bones and filth. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The second pursuit was more modest in size - a woman named Jolanda. The Hag selected her weapon but paused, she only had so many and though she might take the younger woman with her bare hands. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI didn\u2019t come to fight\u201d said Jolanda with a faint German accent. \u201cI have here a document, the terms of your surrender. You have no where to hide, we will keep coming until you\u2019ve run out of tricks, unless you surrender.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Hag gave another of her horrible laughs and fetched out Cynthia's blood. \u201cIs that what you think? One of the kind to another, they will not seek me. This cave will be my prison, and a fitting one it is too, with guards at the gate and when the guards grow old their children will by my jailor, and their children after that.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Not many hunters would have realised what she was trying to do, but Jolanda was one of the rare few. She knew that the Hag\u2019s words would bind fate, ensuring her eventual escape and at least three generations wasted guarding her tomb, but Jolanda also knew that this was a rushed job, it could be stopped if she could think of a better ending by herself in the next minute. Fortunately Jolanda came prepared. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cOne of the kind to another\u201d she spat The Hag\u2019s words back at her \u201cThis is where I repay my debts\u201d. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Jolanda lifted her thumb off the dead man\u2019s switch. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-19-2014, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T17:18:27-07:00","id":93928,"title":"","content":"I am going to line-edit this, if that's ok with you. It's a little clumsy but there is, perhaps, potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T17:22:41-07:00","id":93932,"title":"","content":"At two and a half pages, I think this is the longest bit of WoD fiction I've ever written, and the runner up would be way back in Djinn: the Binding (the first I ever worked on).<br /> <br /> Five cells and 4 additional hunters from five different Compacts were harmed in the making of this story, at a guess I'd say that about a quarter of the hunters who took part in this hunt appeared on screen.<br /> <br /> <br /> The core idea was to show how I always imagined a Hunter vs True Fae showdown would go. You'll notice that when The Hag pulls off a nasty trick she can take down whole squads of hunters in a single action, she did this when she killed Cynthia and again with the bag of wind. To a lesser extent she also did this when she surprised Reverend Benjamin by attacking physically.<br /> <br /> However when she attacks directly she looses. You see this in the fight against the Sons of C\u00fa Chulainn and the fight against The Long Night - in both fights she was loosing badly and only managed to turn the tide by deploying a trick. Her physical strength against the Long Night and surprise reinforcements against the Sons. <br /> <br /> I always imagined that Hunters typically have an advantage over most fae in direct combat - and the fae retaliate with stealth and trickery. The True Fae bump this up to being even with hunters in direct combat, and massively overpower them when they can play to their strengths. The Hag started alone against Hunters with superior positioning and her frailties, yet she survived going toe-to-toe with two cells in direct sequence, not bad at all, yet pathetic to what you see her doing when she plays a trick. The idea of the Hag always having one more trick also ties into the Theme of Dream Catchers, you don't know the rules.<br /> <br /> Note that when I say &quot;even with with hunters&quot;, I mean even with hunters who can occasionally round up a dozen cells or even an air strike. Not &quot;four dudes with shotguns, and maybe an Endowment&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Key players:<ul><li>Maria Carcione and her cell are Union, she's related to Joey Carcione from the Hunter core.</li> <li>Cynthia - I can neither confirm nor deny that Cynthia and her cell are based on my own interpretation of the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, which is identical to cannon save that they all know about and are proud of their witch/thamaturge members. I can also neither confirm nor deny that Cynthia was mostly designed around a convoluted maiden/mother/crone joke.</li> <li>Johnny McDermot and Brother Larry are Sons and both from Dream Catchers (so naturally they have plot armour and survived), the other Hounds are not.</li> <li>Reverend Benjamin, Carter and Jesse are Long Night. Fun fact, they are the first Long Night I've written who aren't from a gospel church. When I think Long Night, <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A3C1zxryK-s\" target=\"_blank\">I think of this</a>.</li> <li>Jolanda is a Loyalist of Thule, her cell was nearby but she got the short straw. Jolanda was almost another Son, but the line about repaying her debt swung it.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> The lack of any Conspiracies contributing is intentional. I believe that if a Conspiracy went up against a True Fae with the kind of advantages the Hunters had here, they'd win without needing alliances. I don't really see the point of having Tiers if Tier 3 isn't significantly more dangerous than Tier 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Hag's Frailties<br /> <br /> If you carve a special symbol into stone and place it on a road, she cannot walk past it while on that road. If all the roads from the hag's present location are warded like this then she cannot leave by any means. This also applies to any minions she creates, but she exploited a loophole by summoning mercenary hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> If she is bound by white lilies by a man of faith then she cannot spend glamour, she also can't remove lillies. The hunters mistakenly thought that blocked all her magic. And yes, this is another maiden/mother/crone joke.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Hag's Tricks<br /> <br /> She's an Ogre Witchtooth.<br /> <br /> Killing Cynthia was just invisibility and the killing blow rule. The spell that turned guns into snakes was probably Wyrd Sorcery with a conditional trigger. Either there was a minuet (and a really good dice roll, which is normal for True Fae with Omens and Hearth) to prepare between the second and third paragraph, or she's pulling a True Fae cheat to cast faster than possible.<br /> <br /> The Manakins are either more Wyrd Sorcery or Contracts of Communion.<br /> <br /> Summoning hobgoblin mercenaries could be Wyrd Sorcery or Contracts of Reflection, Wyrd Sorcery would probably do it better. (She can open a portal to them, she just can't go through it with her frailty)<br /> <br /> Killing Reverend Benjamin was her natural strength, augmented (possibility superfaciously) by Might of the Terrible Brute and it's obliging Catch.<br /> <br /> The fight in the sewer was naturally a Token. Simplest to think of it as a Hedgespun gun with autofire.<br /> <br /> Finally her attempt to bind Fate doesn't really make any sense at all - given that even True Fae level Fate magic can't really bind people to actions when they have all the cards. The use of Cynthia's blood almost makes sense as a substitute for Glamour, Wyrd Sorcery can use material components instead of Glmaour, but only Goblin Fruit. Though this has tempted me to add blood sacrifice as an alternative. Jolanda's counter makes sense if you imagine it interrupted the roll to cast the spell, what the story implies happened - that The Hag rushed the job and basically made it very easy for Jolanda to Twist (&quot;I'll be trapped until it's interesting that I escape&quot; -&gt; &quot;I'll be trapped until there's a more interesting conclusion&quot;) ignores the fact that only a fae or Hedge Witch, which Jolanda is not, can Twist magic and certianly not as an instant action.<br /> <br /> <br /> I plead poetic license.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T17:23:25-07:00","id":93935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/93906-one-more-trick-a-hunter-fiction?p=93928#post93928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to line-edit this, if that's ok with you. It's a little clumsy but there is, perhaps, potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not ok with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T17:25:35-07:00","id":93941,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but I already did. I should not post the final draft?","signature":"","